From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eric R. Smith" <eric.smith@collabora.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Apr 2025 13:23:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost, panvk: spread hierarchy mask bits out when
 max_levels < 8

We create hierarchy masks based on the number of levels available,
creating a bitmask with `max_levels` bits set. Originally these bits
all came together. Modify this to spread the bits out, which improves
performance on chips like the G31 with only 2 levels of hierarchy.

Reviewed-by: Olivia Lee <olivia.lee@collabora.com>
Reviewed-by: Lars-Ivar Hesselberg Simonsen <lars-ivar.simonsen@arm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/34744>
(cherry picked from commit 548f652d101fab0de6facc17465e9d1e254e1544,
 onto pan_util.h, where 25.0 keeps the function)
---
 src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h
index a4b8deb..311892f 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h
@@ -85,7 +85,19 @@ pan_select_tiler_hierarchy_mask(unsigned width, unsigned height,
 {
    uint32_t max_fb_wh = MAX2(width, height);
    uint32_t last_hierarchy_bit = util_last_bit(DIV_ROUND_UP(max_fb_wh, 16));
-   uint32_t hierarchy_mask = BITFIELD_MASK(max_levels);
+   uint32_t hierarchy_mask;
+
+   if (max_levels < 8) {
+      /* spread the bits out somewhat */
+      static uint32_t default_mask[] = {
+         0, 0x80, 0x82, 0xa2,
+         0xaa, 0xea, 0xee, 0xfe
+      };
+      hierarchy_mask = default_mask[max_levels];
+      max_levels = 8; /* the high bit of the mask is always set */
+   } else {
+      hierarchy_mask = BITFIELD_MASK(max_levels);
+   }
 
    /* Always enable the level covering the whole FB, and disable the finest
     * levels if we don't have enough to cover everything.
-- 
